{"name":"Japanese Poet","hex":"#c4bab7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who writes poems.","A person with a creative or romantic imagination."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Japanese poetry","blocks":[{"text":"Japanese poetry is poetry typical of Japan, or written, spoken, or chanted in the Japanese language, which includes Old Japanese, Early Middle Japanese, Late Middle Japanese, and Modern Japanese, as well as poetry in Japan which was written in the Chinese language or ryūka from the Okinawa Islands: it is possible to make a more accurate distinction between Japanese poetry written in Japan or by Japanese people in other languages versus that written in the Japanese language by speaking of Japanese-language poetry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/%27Kokinshu%27-_Anthology_of_Classic_Japanese_Poetry_LACMA_M.91.250.332.jpg/330px-%27Kokinshu%27-_Anthology_of_Classic_Japanese_Poetry_LACMA_M.91.250.332.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_poetry","wikidata":"Q1683305"},{"title":"Poet","blocks":[{"text":"A poet is a person who studies and creates poetry. Poets may describe themselves as such or be described as such by others. A poet might simply be the creator who creates (composes) poems, or someone who also performs their art to an audience."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poet","wikidata":"Q49757"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/32_ban_Shokunin_utaawase_Sanoki-Komoso.JPG/500px-32_ban_Shokunin_utaawase_Sanoki-Komoso.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/32_ban_Shokunin_utaawase_Sanoki-Komoso.JPG/500px-32_ban_Shokunin_utaawase_Sanoki-Komoso.JPG?utm_source=en.wi